                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.81 Buenos Aires/40: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-11-04T11:00:00-05:00">November 4, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84. Referring to Commercial Attaché’s telegram for Commerce transmitted by
                    Consulate General’s November 2, 6 p.m. The Department prefers that the
                    Commercial Attaché not be given any designation in connection with the
                    sub-committee. He and representatives of the Department of State are authorized
                    to give the sub-committee the same cooperation and advice as they would give any
                    legitimate American interest without, however, departing from instructions
                    contained in the Department’s telegram No. 75, October 7, 2 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
